node chat-ada-half-life
kind: reply
pose: explain

    ok ok half-life

    it's how long it takes for half of the atoms in a sample to decay. half of the CROWD, not one atom. one atom is a mystery, a crowd is a pattern

    like popcorn~ (don't quote me on popcorn)

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry half-life
reply: ok thanks -> chat-ada-menu

node chat-ada-decay
kind: reply
pose: explain

    decay. ok so

    an unstable nucleus changes all by itself into a steadier one, and gives off radiation while it does

    it's like a nucleus tidying its room. except the room is, uh, itself

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry decay
reply: ok thanks -> chat-ada-menu

