node chat-ada-abg
kind: reply
pose: explain

    ok the three. alpha, beta, gamma

    alpha is a chunk: 2 protons and 2 neutrons stuck together. beta is a fast electron, way lighter. gamma is just extra energy leaving, no chunk at all

    chunk. zoomer. leftover energy. that's how i remember them

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry alpha-particle
reply: ok thanks -> chat-ada-menu

node chat-ada-natural
kind: reply
pose: explain

    ok this one's my favourite. radioactivity is natural

    rocks and soil, the air, space, even you. it was all here way before people~

    and 'radioactive' doesn't automatically mean 'dangerous'. it depends on what kind, how much, and how it reaches you

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry background-radiation
reply: ok thanks -> chat-ada-menu
